Factors of a Number
What is a Factor?
A factor is a number that divides another number without leaving a remainder

Count Number of Factors
Instead of printing factors, we can count them.

Factorial of a Number
What is Factorial?
Factorial means multiplying a number by all positive numbers below it.

Armstrong Number
What is an Armstrong Number?
For a 3-digit number, if the sum of the cubes of its digits is equal to the original number, it is an Armstrong number.

